 {
  "id": "lean-fit-12wk",
  "name": "Lean & Fit: 12-Week Fat Loss",
  "level": "Beginner",
  "goal": "Lose fat, gain fitness",
  "desc": "Four rides a week (three in easy weeks): one short interval session, one tempo/sweet-spot ride and two easy Zone 2 rides, with the hard days separated. Volume grows from about 3 to 5 hours per week with a lighter week every fourth week, and ramp tests in weeks 1, 5 and 12 keep the intensities right as you get fitter. Fat (including belly fat) comes off the whole body, not one spot: pair the rides with a modest calorie deficit, enough protein, fewer sugary drinks and snacks, good sleep and, ideally, two short strength sessions a week. Aim for about 0.3-0.5 kg per week. Ride the sessions in order and leave a rest or easy day between hard sessions.",
  "src": "Polarized-leaning base (mostly Zone 2) + low-volume HIIT; 3:1 load/recovery",
