  "desc": "Six weeks to get a scout team ready for the 24h vélo du Bois de la Cambre in Brussels, a 24-hour relay where each rider takes turns of 1 to 4 laps (about 5 to 15 minutes hard), again and again through the day and the night. Three 30-60 minute sessions a week fit around school: lap-length efforts with a hard start and a strong finish, relay simulations that teach you to go hard again after resting, short accelerations, and easy Zone 2 rides to recover and build your base. Week 1 starts with a ramp test to set your FTP, week 4 is lighter and week 6 is a taper that ends with a short opener a day or two before race weekend. Pacing a turn: go hard but not all-out on the first lap (sprint for 20-30 seconds after the change, then settle), hold a steady pace you can keep for the whole turn, and only empty the tank in the last few hundred metres before you hand over. Between turns: drink, eat something, put on warm clothes straight away, and at night sleep a little whenever your next turn is more than about two hours away. Ride the sessions in order and leave a rest day between the two hard sessions of the week.",
